# Round glmrescli: GLM-5.3-Flash's decode under adaptive residency on plan (a) (A6000), the same
# binary, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY unset (off) against mid-p33-s1 (33 pinned, 1 spare a layer).
# P: plan (a) holds card experts on the 39 routed layers whose stacks card_routed takes (3-10,
# 13-43; model::arch::glm5next::place::card_routed, placement::plan_routed), n_l = 67 of 288 at
# the fewest [derived, glmtrace.card: 40.09 GB over 39 x 15,204,352 B = 67.6 a layer]; P = 67 / 2
# = 33 (Qwen3.8's rule, bloomery_levers::residency38_at_plan), P + S + 1 = 35 <= 67. The churn
# pool is 39 x (67..68 - 33) = 1,326..1,365 experts, 20.2..20.8 GB beside the host set.
# The step (S1 = 47.7 ms, 20.95 tok/s @ n=96, depth 512, A6000, rig-log 09-28#glm-release): the
# host serves 39 x 8 x (1 - 0.233) + 3 x 8 = 263 routed slots a token at the id prefix (hit ~
# 67 / 288 on prose), 4.0 GB at 130-137 GB/s = 29-31 ms, plus 42 x 60-80 us; a slot is 0.111-0.117
# ms of it [derived]. The card experts run in the host leg's shadow, and stay there at any hit
# below: 5 card slots a layer at ~700 GB/s are 0.11 ms against a 0.40 ms host leg.
# Steady state (ideaverify's replay, 25,424 held-out tokens: mid 63.4 %, 5.24 swaps a token): 312 x
# (0.55..0.634 - 0.233) = 99..125 slots off, 11.0-14.6 ms, less the swaps' DRAM share (80 MB a
# token, three passes, 0-1.8 ms: none if the staging fits the card fronts, all if it meets the
# host leg) = -9.2..-14.6 ms, +24..+44 %.
# This window is not the steady state. The prompt call keeps 0 rows, so the rule learns nothing
# from the 512 ids and starts at the id prefix; it plans every 4 passes, at most 24 flips a pass
# over 39 layers and one a layer in flight, a flip live 2 passes after it is made: at most ~22
# planning passes land inside the 95 timed steps, ~13.5 flips a layer against the ~30 the
# steady state needs. Largest gain first, a local profile as skewed as the replay's (the top 13
# non-pinned experts about 0.35 of a layer's routing) and early passes held back by margin 3:
# the window's mean hit 0.35..0.51, 37..87 slots off, 4.1-10.2 ms, less 0-2.1 ms of swap DRAM
# (the ramp is cap-bound, 6 flips a step) = 2.0-10.2 ms off 47.7: +4..+27 % [derived].
# The measured anchor for the ramp's low edge: ideaverify's V4.1 domain switch under mid, the 64
# steps after it at 56.5 % against 81.3 % steady and 47.2 % static, a quarter of the gain; on GLM
# a quarter of 0.233 -> 0.634 is ~11 points, 34 slots, 3.8 ms, 1.7-3.8 ms net: +3.7..+8.6 %.
# late / wait_us: a planning pass's 24 flips stage on one thread, 24 x 15.2 MB at a one-thread
# copy of 6-12 GB/s = 30-61 ms, inside two steps (74-92 ms at the band's step): late 0 on every
# boundary and wait_us under 1,000 at a landing boundary [derived]. At a one-thread rate of 4
# GB/s (130 GB/s over 32 threads) the pass takes 91 ms: late > 0 at the ramp's landings.
# Prerequisites, none of them in this round's files: the registry word mid-p33-s1
# (crates/levers/src/registry.rs), RESIDENCY_LEVER and RESIDENCY_HOST in GENERATE_GLM5NEXT
# (crates/gpu-gates/src/record.rs, then just records-refresh), and the `<D>@NAME=VALUE` lever
# arm in tools/ref/depth-glm5next.sh (depth-qwen3moe.sh's grammar). Without the last the runner
# refuses the second arm (rc 64) before the lease.
# Runner: BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/glmres-ab.card'
#   just depth-gpu-glm5next 512 512@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p33-s1 > <log> 2>&1
# Wall [derived]: 2 arms x (3 rounds + 1 warm-up), each a load (host set populate, ~1-2 min
# preheated) plus 512 ids and 95 steps (~5 s): 8 processes, 10-18 min.
kind: ab
question: does adaptive residency from the id-prefix seed lift GLM-5.3-Flash's decode on plan (a)
  inside a 96-token window by the ramp model's band?
term: tok/s(mean) @ n=96, depth 512, A6000, plan (a), prose ids (GLM_PROSE from GLM_PROSE_FROM),
  ctx 2048, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p33-s1 against unset, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +4..+27
rounds: 3
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」, same-binary paired ratio SD
condition: one binary, both arms in one lease, a fresh process a run (each residency run starts at
  the seed), each arm's host set preheated and its row not [cold], no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
  row; the residency arm prints `residency lever residency=mid-p33-s1 why=set`, a `residency host`
  record with pinned=33 and headroom_after > 0, and 96 `residency pass` records (pass=none before
  the prompt call, pass=prompt kept=0, then 94 of pass=step kept=1) whose landed sum is > 0; the
  off arm prints no residency record
decide-in: set the GLM default to mid-p<P>-s1 under --place a (P half the plan's fewest, as
  Qwen3.8's), then take the steady-state row at n = 512 with --warm 256 before any public table
decide-below: read the residency pass records: landed near 0 means the margin holds the ramp back
  (the rule's min_count or margin at GLM's width, not the copy); late > 0 or wait_us over 1,000
  means the staging sits on the step: one nsys window of the residency arm before any change
decide-above: the ramp is faster than cap 24 over 4 passes predicts, so the locality is sharper
  than the replay's: re-derive the steady-state band from a longer window (n = 512) before the
  default decision
